                        ],
                        "form": "empaillées"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7d6a5827-f4f4-396a-bd67-0782023a060d",
                        "entry_id": "d753545e-9d7e-3230-a08a-c92d9afa34ea",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rembourré de paille."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e4f2850-94f5-4a34-8f09-601a828e5770",
                                "sense_id": "7d6a5827-f4f4-396a-bd67-0782023a060d",
                                "text": "Un oiseau empaillé."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "34a17d75-2d88-40b5-8dc9-a491f9c4288f",
                                "sense_id": "7d6a5827-f4f4-396a-bd67-0782023a060d",
                                "text": "On voyait des têtes proprement empaillées qu’on allait porter à la Sublime-Porte."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "047a1a11-ba95-3d5c-9d8d-3052b7e57267",
                        "entry_id": "d753545e-9d7e-3230-a08a-c92d9afa34ea",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Défendu par de la paille."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa12a10c-60fc-497e-8ddb-53695058925d",
                                "sense_id": "047a1a11-ba95-3d5c-9d8d-3052b7e57267",
                                "text": "Un figuier empaillé pour l’hiver."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d438b1ad-3a18-33e3-afa6-50b9c00ae536",
                        "entry_id": "d753545e-9d7e-3230-a08a-c92d9afa34ea",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Figé, statique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9a9f902-edc1-48fb-8879-b73f8b9f8663",
                                "sense_id": "d438b1ad-3a18-33e3-afa6-50b9c00ae536",
                                "text": "— Mille millions de tonnerres ! rugit-il, vous êtes donc empaillé, vous ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "921ee6f6-a41b-45cf-8367-9c08ccc72a78",
                                "sense_id": "d438b1ad-3a18-33e3-afa6-50b9c00ae536",
                                "text": "Les façades d’immeubles et les carrefours étaient devenus, au fil des années, un paysage intérieur qui avait fini par recouvrir le Paris trop lisse et empaillé du présent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "759c6f9e-8af1-431d-80c3-1d2896923ee6",
                        "source_entry_id": "d753545e-9d7e-3230-a08a-c92d9afa34ea",
                        "target_lang_word": "stuffed",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stuffed",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "548d5b27-6ba1-3ddd-be87-3e17c524e116",
                                        "entry_id": "105e1061-eed8-3a4a-96b0-c04ecc1c5abf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of stuff"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "stuffed",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                        "entry_id": "870285c1-3196-3b21-a501-907366456ef0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Full or packed (with some material or substance)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e572d084-cacb-4a94-be61-3afa96c5696b",
                                                "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: stuffed to the gills"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d48da13f-b156-48ed-a11e-e0d8d4467aab",
                                                "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                                "text": "Customs officers look closely through a stuffed suitcase."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b9a4454-0598-42d9-b304-fd38b8c0e1d3",
                                                "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                                "text": "They burned the old gun that used to stand in the dark corner up in the garret, close to the stuffed fox that always grinned so fiercely. Perhaps the reason why he seemed in such a ghastly rage was that he did not come by his death fairly. Otherwise his pelt would not have been so perfect. And why else was he put away up there out of sight?—and so magnificent a brush as he had too.[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa9ff101-d581-4ed6-9462-46ee70e5fcff",
                                                "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                                "text": "In unconscious memory of this relationship of animals and innocence, children's rooms are traditionally filled with stuffed animals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "153a887c-58bf-401e-af6c-1cceaa330750",
                                                "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                                "text": "Hence, perhaps, the dins Céline deafens us with, in texts more and more stuffed with onomatopoeias."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1c9e83a-2fc9-428a-a08f-c95b0a996b49",
                                                "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                                "text": "She didn't forget to pack anything, none of those irritating little things that wait till the last moment to pop out of hiding and make her re-open her most stuffed suitcase."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec1bf357-574a-40a9-81aa-3be829feaff3",
                                                "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                                "text": "The more stuffed your hard drive, the more Blob-like it becomes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbcbb364-e15e-4329-b5d9-a0bb9581f1a3",
                                                "sense_id": "54710333-19d1-3409-b4a4-32dc43185c7c",
                                                "text": "Creating a poetic or extraordinary belief is the simple act of intensifying the mood or atmosphere of your belief and making it more stuffed with the ability or power to come real."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28b2bb4c-37da-376b-a0c2-3eb1382e0b67",
                                        "entry_id": "870285c1-3196-3b21-a501-907366456ef0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Filled with a filling and seasoning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f84f1512-b682-41f2-bb8f-984d3665419a",
                                                "sense_id": "28b2bb4c-37da-376b-a0c2-3eb1382e0b67",
                                                "text": "We're having stuffed turkey for dinner."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e290fcb-2691-4866-b761-a0394fd5fac1",
                                                "sense_id": "28b2bb4c-37da-376b-a0c2-3eb1382e0b67",
                                                "text": "The turkey is stuffed with a stuffing made of bread and herbs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e85621e4-3171-3b99-9d90-9db86f1ca640",
                                        "entry_id": "870285c1-3196-3b21-a501-907366456ef0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Full after eating."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1578f47-2401-4335-b695-70075d132545",
                                                "sense_id": "e85621e4-3171-3b99-9d90-9db86f1ca640",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: stuffed to the gills"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13e9dd87-eacf-4e17-b1c5-0e4ed57ac7fd",
                                                "sense_id": "e85621e4-3171-3b99-9d90-9db86f1ca640",
                                                "text": "Stuffed children sleep poorly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01fedc79-c619-4117-ae68-bd4d4f38ef82",
                                                "sense_id": "e85621e4-3171-3b99-9d90-9db86f1ca640",
                                                "text": "Beth says: \"I never knew when I was full 'cause I always felt like I didn't know whether I was hungry or full. My whole life I never knew when I was full or hungry unless I was really stuffed or really starving.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7b1badf-31fb-49ca-9587-87589a6ba9a0",
                                                "sense_id": "e85621e4-3171-3b99-9d90-9db86f1ca640",
                                                "text": "\"See, huge meal.\" Replied Farra. / \"Still stuffed.\" / \"Yes, quite stuffed.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbc2df19-7030-42ab-8394-02f3684da4db",
                                                "sense_id": "e85621e4-3171-3b99-9d90-9db86f1ca640",
                                                "text": "Allhadi gave a contented yawn and said: / \"I have eaten till I am really stuffed / I am full and bloated and so puffed / I am bursting, I am telling you true / I couldn't eat more if you begged me to.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71b9fe6d-a951-3fbd-a057-64c874309da7",
                                        "entry_id": "870285c1-3196-3b21-a501-907366456ef0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very tired."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "New-Zealand",
                                            "UK",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c895a1c7-488a-44a4-a54c-28359c7f21be",
                                                "sense_id": "71b9fe6d-a951-3fbd-a057-64c874309da7",
                                                "text": "'Well, you talked me into it,' said Cornelius. 'I feel really stuffed. I can tell you that for sure. So I could do with a bloody good sleep.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6736c1a1-bb66-3fe7-a991-885431e49138",
                                        "entry_id": "870285c1-3196-3b21-a501-907366456ef0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Broken, not functional; in trouble, in a situation from which one is unlikely to recover."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "New-Zealand",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "810b289b-1d8d-45c1-8a12-aa98d1aa17bd",
                                                "sense_id": "6736c1a1-bb66-3fe7-a991-885431e49138",
                                                "text": "If the suspension was stuffed already from hitting the concrete base of the fence—and it was—then it was really stuffed by the time we'd gone a kilometre along the railway."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3511139-ad92-40ad-830a-6bdfb2300be7",
                                                "sense_id": "6736c1a1-bb66-3fe7-a991-885431e49138",
                                                "text": "But if you don't play ball in life, if you don′t go for it with a sincere 'Go, girrrrl' rugby-tackle attitude, you're really stuffed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a0425e7-4b83-4196-8a6e-d711449b97f5",
                                                "sense_id": "6736c1a1-bb66-3fe7-a991-885431e49138",
                                                "text": "Although the 14-inch Standard that Yamato targets is stuffed, and maybe the one after that, a prolonged bombardment by a Colorado-class is not gonna do good things to anything - doesn't really matter who you are."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6d77834c-b222-48df-9e6e-5b76cf47f202",
                        "source_entry_id": "d753545e-9d7e-3230-a08a-c92d9afa34ea",
